  "headline": "Ousted Leader Sheikh Hasina Sets December 16 Return To Bangladesh",
  "seoTitle": "Sheikh Hasina Plans Return To Bangladesh On December 16",
  "metaDescription": "Former Prime Minister Sheikh Hasina has announced plans to return to Bangladesh on December 16, despite facing a death sentence and government warnings.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "Former Prime Minister Sheikh Hasina has publicly declared her intention to travel to Bangladesh on December 16.",
    "The date coincides with the 55th anniversary of the country's Liberation War, commonly celebrated as Victory Day.",
    "Current government officials stated that Hasina, who faces a death sentence in absentia, would be subject to arrest upon arrival."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "Sheikh Hasina has been living in exile in India for the past two years following her removal from office. Last year, a court in Bangladesh sentenced the former leader to death in absentia for her role in ordering a severe crackdown against a student-led uprising that resulted in hundreds of fatalities. While Hasina has previously expressed a desire to return home, this marks the first time she has specified a date for her homecoming. The Bangladesh government has responded to her request, maintaining that she can only be returned to the country through official extradition procedures. Officials in Dhaka have stated that should she arrive, she would face immediate apprehension, with some members of the administration labeling the request as one that would only result in her return in handcuffs.",
